## How to Choose the Right Halo for an Emerald Cut Diamond

The decision comes down to one question: do you want the halo visible from above, or invisible from above?

If visible from above — choose the [Pavé Diamond Halo at $1,520](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-cushion-emerald-radiant-by-james-allen-item-314929?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (entry, 69 reviews, rectangular outline) or the [Falling Edge Pavé Halo](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/falling-edge-pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311110?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) ($2,410–$3,010, 369 reviews, most validated). Both follow the rectangular outline.

If invisible from above — choose the [X Split Shank Hidden Halo at $3,040](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/x-split-shank-hidden-halo-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-2-ct-tw-item-192267?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The stone's rectangle is completely untouched. The halo sparkle is a side-view feature only.

> "I always tell buyers to look at the ring from directly above — the engagement position. That is the view your partner sees most. If the ring reads as a clean, elegant emerald cut from above, you have chosen the right halo. If the ring reads as a round or oval because the halo overpowers the stone's outline, you have chosen the wrong one." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

What to avoid: any halo described only as "round" or "oval" without shape-specific compatibility for the emerald cut. Halos designed for round brilliant stones use a circular perimeter. That circular perimeter is exactly what The Outline Problem describes.

A halo that a retailer lists as "works with all shapes" almost always means round-designed. Shape-specific compatibility matters — check before buying.

Check the product listing for specific mentions of cushion, emerald, or radiant compatibility. The [Pavé Diamond Halo (EC/Cushion/Radiant)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-cushion-emerald-radiant-by-james-allen-item-314929?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) names these shapes in the product title. That is the signal you need.

